WEBVTT

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:10.387
REX: Hey, Buzz! Stop!

00:00:10.627 --> 00:00:12.067
Slow down!

00:00:13.427 --> 00:00:16.987
To overnight six packages
to Japan is how much?

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.267
-(WOMAN SPEAKING, INDISTINCT)
-That's in yen, right?

00:00:19.347 --> 00:00:22.627
Dollars? (GROANS)
You are deliberately taking advantage

00:00:22.707 --> 00:00:24.747
of people in a hurry, you know that?

00:00:24.827 --> 00:00:27.787
All right. (SPUTTERING)
I'll do it! All right. Fine.

00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:31.027
I'll have the stuff in the lobby,
and you'd better be here in 15 minutes,

00:00:31.107 --> 00:00:34.027
because I have a plane
to catch, do you hear me?

00:00:34.107 --> 00:00:36.467
-(DOOR CLOSING)
-Whoo-hoo! -(DOOR CLOSING)
-Whoo-hoo!

00:00:36.547 --> 00:00:39.587
We're finally going.
Can you believe it?

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:41.867
(LAUGHS) That's custom-fitted

00:00:41.947 --> 00:00:43.867
foam insulation
you'll be riding in, Bullseye.

00:00:43.947 --> 00:00:45.427
First class all the way!

00:00:46.187 --> 00:00:49.747
You know what?
I'm actually excited about this.

00:00:49.827 --> 00:00:51.787
I mean it. I really am!

00:00:51.867 --> 00:00:54.387
-And why shouldn't you be?
-Yee-haw!

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.747
-Whoa!
-♪ Swing your partner do-si-do ♪

00:00:56.827 --> 00:01:01.267
-Look at you, dancing cowboy!
-Look! I'm doin' the box step!

00:01:01.387 --> 00:01:02.667
(PETE LAUGHS)

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:04.667
(GRUNTING)

00:01:11.787 --> 00:01:13.827
Uh-oh. Hey, heads up down there!

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:18.787
-Whoa! Pork bellies are fallin'.
-Hey, how much farther, Buzz?

00:01:18.907 --> 00:01:21.547
(GRUNTING) Halfway there.

00:01:21.627 --> 00:01:25.307
(GROANING)
My arms can't hold on much longer!

00:01:25.387 --> 00:01:26.547
(TOYS CRYING OUT)

00:01:29.827 --> 00:01:31.827
(GRUNTING) Too heavy.

00:01:32.387 --> 00:01:33.427
What was I thinking?

00:01:33.547 --> 00:01:36.547
-My antigravity servos!
-(HYDRAULIC WHIRRING)

00:01:36.627 --> 00:01:40.027
Hang tight, everyone.
I'm going to let go of the wall.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.667
-What?
-He wouldn't.

00:01:41.747 --> 00:01:43.547
-One...
-He would.

00:01:43.627 --> 00:01:45.787
-Two...
-(ALL PROTEST)

00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:47.827
-Three!
-(TOYS SCREAMING)

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:49.827
(TOYS LANDING, GRUNTING)

00:01:50.347 --> 00:01:54.347
To infinity and beyond!

00:01:56.427 --> 00:01:59.387
Approaching destination.
Reengaging gravity.

00:02:00.187 --> 00:02:01.427
(HYDRAULIC WHIRRING)

00:02:05.507 --> 00:02:07.067
(LASER BUZZING)

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:10.507
-Area secure.
-(ALL MOANING)

00:02:10.787 --> 00:02:11.787
It's okay, troops.

00:02:11.867 --> 00:02:16.267
The antigravity sickness will wear off
momentarily. Now let's move!

00:02:16.867 --> 00:02:20.187
Remind me to glue his helmet shut
when we get back.

00:02:29.307 --> 00:02:31.387
How 'bout givin' me
a little intro there, Jessie?

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:35.107
Introducing the high-ridin'-est
cowboy around...

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:37.147
-You forgot "rootin'-tootin'-est"!
-(GIGGLES)

00:02:37.227 --> 00:02:41.147
The high-ridin'-est, rootin'-tootin'-est
cowboy hero of all time,

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.547
Sheriff Woody!

00:02:52.347 --> 00:02:55.947
Say, little missy, you notice
any trouble around these parts?

00:02:56.027 --> 00:02:58.747
Nary a bit,
not with Sheriff Woody around.

00:02:58.827 --> 00:03:00.747
Wait, wait, wait! I got it!
This is great! Okay!

00:03:00.827 --> 00:03:03.507
The bandits got the critters tied up
in the burning barn. Now the best part!

00:03:03.587 --> 00:03:05.587
Help us! The barn's on fire!

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.907
I've got ya, critters. No need to worry.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:10.347
Woody saves the day again!

00:03:10.427 --> 00:03:11.587
Yee-haw!

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:13.627
Now, where's my trusty steed Bullseye?

00:03:13.707 --> 00:03:16.267
I have to ride off into the sunset...
Oh!

00:03:16.347 --> 00:03:19.747
Ride like the wind, Bullseye!
(GRUNTS)

00:03:21.787 --> 00:03:23.907
(GROANS, CHUCKLES)

00:03:24.587 --> 00:03:26.707
(GIGGLING) Watch it.
Wait. I'm ticklish, okay?

00:03:26.827 --> 00:03:28.387
Oh, you are?

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.707
No, no, no. Cut it out.
Stop it. Stop it.

00:03:30.787 --> 00:03:32.627
-No, please. No, no. Stop! Stop!
-(LAUGHING)

00:03:38.587 --> 00:03:39.827
(LASER BUZZING)

00:03:42.907 --> 00:03:45.067
Mission log. Have reached
Zurg's command deck,

00:03:45.147 --> 00:03:47.787
but no sign of him
or his wooden captive.

00:03:47.867 --> 00:03:50.427
-WOODY: Please, no!
-That's Woody!

00:03:50.507 --> 00:03:52.507
-(HOWLING)
-This way!

00:03:55.867 --> 00:03:57.827
WOODY: Please, please, no!

00:03:57.907 --> 00:03:59.787
POTATO HEAD: Buzz, can you see?
What's going on?

00:03:59.867 --> 00:04:01.147
(SHOUTING, PROTESTS CONTINUE)

00:04:01.747 --> 00:04:04.307
JESSIE: Take that!
POTATO HEAD: To the left.

00:04:04.387 --> 00:04:05.587
No, your left.

00:04:05.827 --> 00:04:07.627
-Take it up higher.
-BUZZ: What's happening?

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:10.787
Oh, it's horrible.
They... They're torturing him.

00:04:10.867 --> 00:04:12.907
(GASPS) What are we gonna do, Buzz?

00:04:12.987 --> 00:04:14.067
Use your head!

00:04:14.867 --> 00:04:17.147
But I don't wanna use my head!

00:04:17.427 --> 00:04:18.707
(ALL SCREAMING)

00:04:21.787 --> 00:04:24.067
-(ALL MOANING)
-What's going on here?

00:04:24.147 --> 00:04:26.307
Buzz, guys!
Hey, how did you find me?

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:27.547
Watch yourself!

00:04:27.627 --> 00:04:29.347
SLINKY: We're here
to spring ya, Woody!

00:04:29.427 --> 00:04:31.267
-(YELLING)
-You heard of kung fu?

00:04:31.347 --> 00:04:33.067
Well, get ready for pork chop.

00:04:33.507 --> 00:04:37.947
Prepare to meet Mr. Angry Eyes!
(SNARLING)

00:04:38.587 --> 00:04:40.307
Hold it, now!
Hey, you don't understand!

00:04:40.387 --> 00:04:41.427
These are my friends!

00:04:41.507 --> 00:04:44.707
-Yeah, we're his friends!
-No, Rex, I mean they're my friends!

00:04:44.787 --> 00:04:45.987
-(GROWLING)
-Hey, stop it!

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:48.947
Leave him alone, springy dog! Hey!

00:04:49.027 --> 00:04:52.507
-Grab Woody, and let's go!
-Fellas, hold it! Buzz, put me down!

00:04:52.587 --> 00:04:54.867
-Quick! To the vent!
-They're stealing him.

00:04:54.947 --> 00:04:56.987
-PETE: No!
-(WOODY YELLING)

00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:58.547
Hold it right there!

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:00.307
-Buzz?
-You again?

00:05:00.387 --> 00:05:03.307
-Thank goodness you're all right.
-Buzz, what is going on?

00:05:03.427 --> 00:05:06.987
Hold on. I am Buzz Lightyear,
and I'm in charge of this detachment.

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:08.467
No, I'm Buzz Lightyear.

00:05:08.547 --> 00:05:10.187
-I'm Buzz Lightyear!
-I'm Buzz Lightyear!

00:05:10.307 --> 00:05:12.147
So, who's the real Buzz?

00:05:12.227 --> 00:05:14.747
-I am!
-Don't let this impostor fool you!

00:05:14.827 --> 00:05:18.267
He's been trained by Zurg himself
to mimic my every move.

00:05:18.347 --> 00:05:20.187
(GASPS, CHOKES)

00:05:21.547 --> 00:05:22.827
(CONTINUES GASPING)

00:05:25.147 --> 00:05:26.147
ALL: Buzz!

00:05:26.227 --> 00:05:27.747
I had a feelin' it was you.

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:31.187
My front end just had
to catch up with my back end.

00:05:31.627 --> 00:05:34.067
Will somebody please
explain what's going on?

00:05:34.147 --> 00:05:37.147
It's all right, Space Ranger.
It's a code 546.

00:05:37.227 --> 00:05:39.947
-(GASPS) You mean it's a...
-Yes.

00:05:40.027 --> 00:05:42.307
-And he's a... (GASPS)
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:46.547
-Your Majesty.
-(CHUCKLES)

00:05:46.627 --> 00:05:48.627
Woody, you're in danger here.
We need to leave now.

00:05:48.707 --> 00:05:50.507
Al's selling you to a toy museum

00:05:50.587 --> 00:05:52.467
-in Japan!
-(CHUCKLING) I know.

00:05:52.547 --> 00:05:55.627
It's okay, Buzz. I actually wanna go.

00:05:55.707 --> 00:05:57.107
-What?
-Are you crazy?

00:05:57.227 --> 00:06:00.307
Look, the thing is,
I'm a rare Sheriff Woody doll,

00:06:00.387 --> 00:06:02.507
and these guys are my Roundup gang.

00:06:02.587 --> 00:06:06.107
-What are you talking about?
-Woody's Roundup!

00:06:06.187 --> 00:06:09.747
Oh, it's this great old TV show,
and I was the star. See? Now look.

00:06:09.827 --> 00:06:12.267
Look! Look at me! See? That's me!

00:06:12.707 --> 00:06:16.067
-This is weirdin' me out.
-Buzz, it was a national phenomenon.

00:06:16.147 --> 00:06:17.907
There was all this merchandise
that got packed up.

00:06:17.987 --> 00:06:19.187
You should have seen it.

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:22.187
There was a record player and a yo-yo.
Buzz, I was a yo-yo!

00:06:22.267 --> 00:06:25.307
-"Was"?
-Stop this nonsense and let's go.

00:06:25.387 --> 00:06:28.707
Nah, Buzz. (SIGHS)

00:06:28.787 --> 00:06:32.147
I can't go. I can't abandon these guys.

00:06:32.227 --> 00:06:34.547
They need me to get into this museum.

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:38.307
Without me, they'll go back
into storage. Maybe forever!

00:06:38.747 --> 00:06:42.387
Woody, you're not a collector's item.
You're a child's plaything.

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:44.907
You are a toy!

00:06:45.027 --> 00:06:48.587
For how much longer? One more rip,
and Andy's done with me.

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:50.987
And what do I do then, Buzz?
Huh? You tell me.

00:06:51.987 --> 00:06:54.387
Somewhere in that pad of stuffing
is a toy who taught me

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:57.667
that life's only worth living
if you're bein' loved by a kid.

00:06:58.267 --> 00:07:01.227
And I traveled all this way
to rescue that toy

00:07:01.307 --> 00:07:03.267
because I believed him.

00:07:04.227 --> 00:07:06.187
Well, you wasted your time.

00:07:12.107 --> 00:07:14.827
-Let's go, everyone.
-What about Woody?

00:07:15.987 --> 00:07:17.747
He's not coming with us.

00:07:19.427 --> 00:07:22.507
But... But Andy's coming home tonight.

00:07:22.587 --> 00:07:25.667
Then we'd better make sure
we're there waiting for him.

